body:
On Studio's `/login` (and any unauthenticated state) the AI chat toggle was visible, and the pre-auth loading spinner rendered flush to the left edge instead of centered.

### Root causes
- `<AiChatPanel />` was rendered unconditionally in `__root.tsx`, outside any session gate.
- `SidebarProvider` wraps children in a row-flex (`flex h-svh w-full`). The loading container used `flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center` with no width, so as a flex item it shrank to content width — `justify-center` centered the spinner only within that shrink-wrapped box.

### Changes (`apps/studio/src/routes/__root.tsx`)
- **Gate the chat panel on auth**: introduce `AuthedAiChatPanel` that consumes `useSession()` inside the existing `SessionProvider` and returns `null` when `user` is absent. Replaces the direct `<AiChatPanel />` render.
- **Fix spinner centering**: add `w-full flex-1` to the `RequireAuth` loading container so it fills `SidebarProvider`'s flex row, making `justify-center` effective horizontally.

```tsx
function AuthedAiChatPanel() {
  const { user } = useSession();
  if (!user) return null;
  return <AiChatPanel />;
}

// loading container
<div className="flex min-h-screen w-full flex-1 items-center justify-center bg-background">
  <div className="h-8 w-8 animate-spin rounded-full border-4 border-muted border-t-primary" />
</div>
```

The `RootComponent`-level "Connecting to ObjectStack…" spinner renders *outside* `SidebarProvider` and was already correctly centered — left untouched.
